1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,470
Namaste dosto, aur
Module 2 mein aapka swagat hai.

2
00:00:04,690 --> 00:00:08,779
Module 1 mein humne Python
ki strong foundation banayi thi.

3
00:00:08,999 --> 00:00:15,447
Ab hum uss engine ko samjhenge jo har AI
agent ke andar chalta hai: large language

4
00:00:15,447 --> 00:00:17,412
model, ya short mein LLM.

5
00:00:17,632 --> 00:00:23,104
Code likhne se pehle ek clear picture
banana zaroori hai, ki yeh model actually kya

6
00:00:23,104 --> 00:00:25,082
karta hai, aur kya nahi karta.

7
00:00:26,382 --> 00:00:32,223
Iss lesson ke baad aap next token
prediction ko simple words mein explain kar paoge.

8
00:00:32,573 --> 00:00:38,514
Aap samjhoge ki tokens kya hote hain, aur
yeh cost, limits aur speed ko kaise decide

9
00:00:38,514 --> 00:00:39,292
karte hain.

10
00:00:39,642 --> 00:00:43,044
Context window kya hai,
aur usme kya kya jaata hai.

11
00:00:43,394 --> 00:00:47,943
Aur model ko control karne ke
liye aapke paas kaun se options hain.

12
00:00:49,243 --> 00:00:52,167
Chalo ek simple
example se shuru karte hain.

13
00:00:52,387 --> 00:00:54,524
Aapke phone ka keyboard dekho.

14
00:00:54,744 --> 00:00:59,622
Aap type karte ho, Happy birthday
to, aur keyboard suggest karta hai, you.

15
00:00:59,842 --> 00:01:02,360
Keyboard ne koi fact look up nahi kiya.

16
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:07,309
Usne bas patterns dekhe hain, ki
iss text ke baad usually kya aata hai.

17
00:01:07,659 --> 00:01:12,112
LLM bhi basically yahi karta
hai, bas bahut bade scale par.

18
00:01:12,332 --> 00:01:15,335
Usne training mein
bahut saara text padha hai.

19
00:01:15,685 --> 00:01:20,750
Aur woh baar baar predict karta hai
ki agla piece of text kya hona chahiye.

20
00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:24,829
Ab yahi idea thoda
technically dekhte hain.

21
00:01:25,179 --> 00:01:28,287
Model ko input milta hai, ab tak ka text.

22
00:01:28,507 --> 00:01:30,201
Jaise, Agents call.

23
00:01:30,421 --> 00:01:34,473
Model ke andar billions of
numbers hain, jinhe weights kehte hain.

24
00:01:34,693 --> 00:01:38,602
Training ke time pe yeh weights
text ke patterns seekh lete hain.

25
00:01:38,952 --> 00:01:41,965
Model ka output poora answer nahi hota.

26
00:01:42,185 --> 00:01:46,239
Output hota hai har
possible next token ki probability.

27
00:01:46,459 --> 00:01:50,977
Jaise, tools ke chances
bahut zyada, APIs ke thode kam.

28
00:01:51,197 --> 00:01:53,724
Yeh numbers sirf samjhane ke liye hain.

29
00:01:54,074 --> 00:01:59,784
Phir ek token choose hota hai, text ke
end mein jud jaata hai, aur poora text wapas

30
00:01:59,784 --> 00:02:03,568
model mein jaata hai, agla
token predict karne ke liye.

31
00:02:03,788 --> 00:02:08,638
Ek lamba answer bas yahi loop hai,
jo sainkdon ya hazaaron baar chalta hai.

32
00:02:09,938 --> 00:02:12,275
Iss process ka dry run karte hain.

33
00:02:12,495 --> 00:02:14,706
Step one: text hai, Agents call.

34
00:02:14,926 --> 00:02:19,029
Sabse likely next token hai
tools, toh woh add ho jaata hai.

35
00:02:19,379 --> 00:02:22,291
Step two: ab text hai, Agents call tools.

36
00:02:22,511 --> 00:02:24,566
Agla likely token hai, to.

37
00:02:24,916 --> 00:02:28,935
Step three: Agents call
tools to, aur agla token hai, act.

38
00:02:29,285 --> 00:02:34,574
Step four: full stop aata hai, aur
model decide karta hai ki answer complete hai.

39
00:02:34,794 --> 00:02:37,099
Yahan generation ruk jaata hai.

40
00:02:38,399 --> 00:02:41,806
Iss loop se ek bahut
important baat samajh aati hai.

41
00:02:42,026 --> 00:02:45,944
Model plausible text likhta
hai, yaani jo sahi lagta hai.

42
00:02:46,164 --> 00:02:48,333
Woh facts look up nahi karta.

43
00:02:48,553 --> 00:02:53,076
Isliye model kabhi kabhi
confidently galat answer de sakta hai.

44
00:02:53,296 --> 00:02:55,512
Isse hallucination kehte hain.

45
00:02:55,732 --> 00:03:00,613
Aur uski knowledge ek date tak hi
hoti hai, jise training cut off kehte hain.

46
00:03:00,833 --> 00:03:06,257
Yahi reason hai ki agents ko tools aur
documents diye jaate hain, taaki woh facts

47
00:03:06,257 --> 00:03:07,395
check kar sakein.

48
00:03:07,615 --> 00:03:09,986
Yeh poora course wahi sikhata hai.

49
00:03:11,286 --> 00:03:13,758
Ab sabse important word: token.

50
00:03:13,978 --> 00:03:15,280
Token kya hai?

51
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,149
Token text ka ek chhota tukda hai.

52
00:03:18,369 --> 00:03:23,631
Kabhi ek poora chhota word, kabhi
kisi lambe word ka hissa, kabhi space ya

53
00:03:23,631 --> 00:03:24,485
punctuation.

54
00:03:24,835 --> 00:03:27,444
Jaise, Agents call tools, full stop.

55
00:03:27,664 --> 00:03:30,293
Yeh shayad chaar tokens mein toot jaaye.

56
00:03:30,513 --> 00:03:32,464
Yeh sirf ek example hai.

57
00:03:32,684 --> 00:03:36,779
Exact split har model ke
tokenizer par depend karta hai.

58
00:03:37,129 --> 00:03:42,392
English text ke liye ek rough rule
hai: lagbhag chaar characters ka ek token.

59
00:03:42,612 --> 00:03:48,451
Code, unusual words, aur Hindi jaisi
doosri languages mein same text ke liye zyada

60
00:03:48,451 --> 00:03:49,733
tokens lagte hain.

61
00:03:50,083 --> 00:03:53,225
Jab exact number
chahiye, toh guess mat karo.

62
00:03:53,445 --> 00:03:59,558
API ke paas ek token counting endpoint
hai, jo aapke exact model ke liye tokens

63
00:03:59,558 --> 00:04:00,332
ginta hai.

64
00:04:00,552 --> 00:04:03,163
Lesson five mein hum isse use karenge.

65
00:04:04,463 --> 00:04:07,464
Tokens ko ek taxi meter ki tarah socho.

66
00:04:07,684 --> 00:04:11,079
Taxi kilometre ke
hisaab se charge karti hai.

67
00:04:11,299 --> 00:04:14,695
API token ke hisaab se charge karti hai.

68
00:04:14,915 --> 00:04:17,822
Aap jo bhejte ho, woh input tokens hain.

69
00:04:18,042 --> 00:04:21,104
Model jo likhta hai,
woh output tokens hain.

70
00:04:21,324 --> 00:04:24,725
Aur output tokens
usually kaafi mehenge hote hain.

71
00:04:26,025 --> 00:04:29,758
Toh tokens aapke liye teen
reasons se matter karte hain.

72
00:04:29,978 --> 00:04:31,175
Pehla, cost.

73
00:04:31,395 --> 00:04:34,644
Har input aur output
token ka paisa lagta hai.

74
00:04:34,994 --> 00:04:36,321
Doosra, limits.

75
00:04:36,541 --> 00:04:41,737
Har request ka ek maximum size hota
hai, jo tokens mein measure hota hai.

76
00:04:42,087 --> 00:04:43,560
Aur teesra, speed.

77
00:04:43,780 --> 00:04:49,025
Reply ek ek token karke banta hai,
toh lamba answer zyada time leta hai.

78
00:04:49,245 --> 00:04:52,721
Lesson four mein
streaming se iska solution dekhenge.

79
00:04:54,021 --> 00:04:55,656
Ab context window.

80
00:04:55,876 --> 00:04:58,468
Isse exam ki desk ki tarah socho.

81
00:04:58,688 --> 00:05:04,062
Exam mein aap sirf wahi use kar sakte
ho jo aapki desk par hai: question paper,

82
00:05:04,062 --> 00:05:06,103
rough sheet, aur answer sheet.

83
00:05:06,323 --> 00:05:10,587
Model bhi sirf wahi dekh
sakta hai jo request ke andar hai.

84
00:05:10,807 --> 00:05:14,508
Aur uska answer bhi usi
desk par fit hona chahiye.

85
00:05:15,808 --> 00:05:21,401
Technically, context window ka matlab
hai: ek request mein model maximum kitne

86
00:05:21,401 --> 00:05:25,703
tokens consider kar sakta
hai, input aur output dono milake.

87
00:05:26,053 --> 00:05:29,086
Jo bhi aap bhejte ho, sab isme jaata hai.

88
00:05:29,306 --> 00:05:32,183
System prompt, yaani aapki instructions.

89
00:05:32,403 --> 00:05:34,508
Ab tak ki poori conversation.

90
00:05:34,728 --> 00:05:37,036
Koi documents ya tool results.

91
00:05:37,256 --> 00:05:38,684
Aur naya message.

92
00:05:39,034 --> 00:05:41,616
Aaj ke models ki window bahut badi hai.

93
00:05:41,836 --> 00:05:48,270
Claude Opus 5.5, jo model hum iss course
mein use karenge, ek million tokens tak le

94
00:05:48,270 --> 00:05:49,045
sakta hai.

95
00:05:49,395 --> 00:05:55,231
Reply ko bhi fit hona padta hai, aur
uski apni limit hai: iss model par ek lakh

96
00:05:55,231 --> 00:05:57,743
atthaais hazaar output tokens tak.

97
00:05:58,093 --> 00:06:02,415
Lekin badi window ka matlab
yeh nahi ki usse poora bhar do.

98
00:06:02,635 --> 00:06:06,060
Har request mein bheja
gaya har token bill hota hai.

99
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:10,310
Aur focused context se
usually answers bhi better aate hain.

100
00:06:10,530 --> 00:06:15,533
Window mein kya jaaye, yeh decide
karna ek core agent engineering skill hai.

101
00:06:16,833 --> 00:06:18,709
Ab ek aur crucial baat.

102
00:06:18,929 --> 00:06:24,920
Imagine karo ek doctor, jo har patient ko
bhool jaata hai jaise hi woh room se bahar

103
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:25,634
jaata hai.

104
00:06:25,854 --> 00:06:31,300
Achhi advice chahiye, toh har visit
par apni poori file saath le jaani padegi.

105
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:33,291
Model wahi doctor hai.

106
00:06:33,511 --> 00:06:36,341
Aur file le jaane ka
kaam aapki app ka hai.

107
00:06:37,641 --> 00:06:43,440
Jab aap kisi chatbot se baat karte ho,
lagta hai ki usse yaad hai aapne pehle kya

108
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:44,085
bola tha.

109
00:06:44,435 --> 00:06:48,777
Lekin model ke paas requests
ke beech koi memory nahi hoti.

110
00:06:48,997 --> 00:06:52,349
Aapki app har baar
poori conversation bhejti hai.

111
00:06:52,569 --> 00:06:55,875
Chat karte waqt model ke
weights change nahi hote.

112
00:06:56,095 --> 00:07:00,131
Agar code history bhejna
bhool gaya, toh conversation gayi.

113
00:07:00,351 --> 00:07:03,595
Lesson three mein aap
yeh khud hote hue dekhoge.

114
00:07:04,895 --> 00:07:07,167
Toh model ko control kaise karein?

115
00:07:07,387 --> 00:07:09,535
Pehla lever hai system prompt.

116
00:07:09,755 --> 00:07:12,855
Isse aap role, rules
aur style set karte ho.

117
00:07:13,205 --> 00:07:17,266
Max tokens se aap reply ki
maximum length set karte ho.

118
00:07:17,616 --> 00:07:22,643
Effort se decide hota hai model
kitna sochega, low se lekar max tak.

119
00:07:22,863 --> 00:07:28,420
Zyada effort mein mushkil problems par
better answers milte hain, lekin tokens bhi

120
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:29,572
zyada lagte hain.

121
00:07:29,922 --> 00:07:33,708
Aur aap model choose karte
ho: Opus, Sonnet, ya Haiku.

122
00:07:33,928 --> 00:07:37,175
Yeh capability aur cost
ke beech ka trade off hai.

123
00:07:37,525 --> 00:07:38,555
Ek note.

124
00:07:38,775 --> 00:07:43,985
Purane tutorials mein aapne
temperature aur top p ke baare mein padha hoga.

125
00:07:44,205 --> 00:07:48,646
Current Claude models par yeh
sampling settings ab accept nahi hoti.

126
00:07:48,866 --> 00:07:53,756
Aap model ko instructions, effort,
aur model choice se steer karte ho.

127
00:07:55,056 --> 00:07:56,515
Interview corner.

128
00:07:56,735 --> 00:08:01,890
Yeh question bahut common hai: ek
LLM text kaise generate karta hai?

129
00:08:02,110 --> 00:08:04,722
Pause karke socho, aap kya bologe.

130
00:08:07,072 --> 00:08:12,664
Ek achha answer: model ab tak ke text
se next token predict karta hai, usse add

131
00:08:12,664 --> 00:08:17,053
karta hai, aur repeat karta
hai jab tak answer complete na ho.

132
00:08:17,273 --> 00:08:21,878
Aur trap se bachna: yeh mat
bolna ki woh internet search karta hai.

133
00:08:22,098 --> 00:08:24,492
Akele model aisa nahi karta.

134
00:08:24,842 --> 00:08:30,526
Doosra question: agar model ki memory
nahi hai, toh chatbot pichle messages kaise

135
00:08:30,526 --> 00:08:31,649
yaad rakhta hai?

136
00:08:33,999 --> 00:08:39,636
Answer: kyunki application har request
ke saath poori history dobara bhejti hai.

137
00:08:39,856 --> 00:08:43,007
API stateless hai, memory app ke paas hai.

138
00:08:43,227 --> 00:08:46,399
Trap: yeh mat bolna ki
model chat se seekhta hai.

139
00:08:46,619 --> 00:08:48,765
Uske weights change nahi hote.

140
00:08:50,065 --> 00:08:51,704
Ab practice ka time.

141
00:08:51,924 --> 00:08:54,676
Yeh questions easy
se hard order mein hain.

142
00:08:54,896 --> 00:08:57,132
Video pause karo aur khud socho.

143
00:08:57,482 --> 00:09:01,197
Pehla: ek LLM
confidently galat kyun ho sakta hai?

144
00:09:01,547 --> 00:09:06,945
Doosra: chaar sau characters ka English
paragraph, roughly kitne tokens ka hoga?

145
00:09:07,295 --> 00:09:12,139
Teesra: aapki chat app har turn
mein pachaas purane messages bhejti hai.

146
00:09:12,359 --> 00:09:13,945
Do problems batao.

147
00:09:14,295 --> 00:09:20,012
Aur chautha, ek real world scenario: ek
support bot ko teen sau page ke manual se

148
00:09:20,012 --> 00:09:21,141
answer dena hai.

149
00:09:21,361 --> 00:09:25,298
Har request mein poora manual
paste kyun nahi karna chahiye?

150
00:09:31,648 --> 00:09:36,615
Hints: plausible text, chaar
characters ka rule, cost aur context window.

151
00:09:36,835 --> 00:09:39,319
Answers quiz dot md file mein hain.

152
00:09:40,619 --> 00:09:41,547
Quick check.

153
00:09:41,767 --> 00:09:46,243
Aapki app ek nayi request
bhejti hai, bina pichle messages ke.

154
00:09:46,463 --> 00:09:47,535
Kya hoga?

155
00:09:53,235 --> 00:09:55,388
Model ko pata hi nahi hoga.

156
00:09:55,608 --> 00:09:58,832
Requests ke beech
uski koi memory nahi hoti.

157
00:09:59,052 --> 00:10:03,014
Woh sirf wahi dekhta hai jo
uss request mein bheja gaya.

158
00:10:04,314 --> 00:10:05,731
Recap karte hain.

159
00:10:05,951 --> 00:10:09,482
LLM next token predict
karta hai, ek loop mein.

160
00:10:09,832 --> 00:10:13,081
Woh plausible text
likhta hai, checked facts nahi.

161
00:10:13,301 --> 00:10:16,420
Isliye important
claims check karne padte hain.

162
00:10:16,770 --> 00:10:20,299
Tokens se cost, limits
aur speed decide hoti hai.

163
00:10:20,649 --> 00:10:25,974
Sab kuch context window mein fit hona
chahiye, aur app har baar history dobara

164
00:10:25,974 --> 00:10:26,725
bhejti hai.

165
00:10:27,075 --> 00:10:33,254
Agle lesson mein aap apni pehli real API
call karoge, aur uske response ka har hissa

166
00:10:33,254 --> 00:10:33,916
samjhoge.

167
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:39,188
Ab time hai Python se ek
model ke saath baat karne ka.

168
00:10:39,408 --> 00:10:44,680
Iss lesson mein hum pehle samjhenge
ki API kya hoti hai aur kyun hoti hai.

169
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:51,042
Phir API key ko safely set karenge,
official Anthropic SDK install karenge, pehla

170
00:10:51,042 --> 00:10:55,820
message bhejenge, aur response
ka har ek hissa kholke dekhenge.

171
00:10:57,120 --> 00:11:02,960
Iss lesson ke baad aap API ko ek
simple analogy ke saath explain kar paoge.

172
00:11:03,310 --> 00:11:07,165
API key ko safely create
aur store karna seekhoge.

173
00:11:07,515 --> 00:11:10,556
Messages dot create se request bhejoge.

174
00:11:10,906 --> 00:11:15,500
Aur response ko padhoge:
content blocks, stop reason, aur usage.

175
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:18,694
Pehle what: API kya hai?

176
00:11:18,914 --> 00:11:21,019
Ek restaurant imagine karo.

177
00:11:21,239 --> 00:11:23,598
Aap seedhe kitchen mein nahi jaate.

178
00:11:23,818 --> 00:11:29,444
Aap waiter ko order dete ho, waiter
kitchen tak order le jaata hai, aur khana wapas

179
00:11:29,444 --> 00:11:30,122
laata hai.

180
00:11:30,472 --> 00:11:32,656
Aapka Python code customer hai.

181
00:11:32,876 --> 00:11:34,348
Order hai request.

182
00:11:34,698 --> 00:11:36,321
API waiter hai.

183
00:11:36,541 --> 00:11:40,995
Waiter ke paas order lene ke
fixed rules hote hain, jaise menu.

184
00:11:41,345 --> 00:11:43,352
Aur model ke servers kitchen hain.

185
00:11:43,572 --> 00:11:46,515
Jo khana wapas aata hai, woh response hai.

186
00:11:46,865 --> 00:11:48,968
Ab why: API kyun hoti hai?

187
00:11:49,188 --> 00:11:53,948
Kyunki model bahut bade servers
par chalta hai, aapke laptop par nahi.

188
00:11:54,168 --> 00:12:00,406
API ek fixed, safe tareeka deti hai,
taaki koi bhi program un servers se baat kar

189
00:12:00,406 --> 00:12:00,791
sake.

190
00:12:02,091 --> 00:12:03,562
Ab API key.

191
00:12:03,782 --> 00:12:06,998
Pehle Claude Console
mein ek API key banao.

192
00:12:07,218 --> 00:12:11,719
Dhyan rahe, API ka billing
chat subscription se alag hota hai.

193
00:12:12,069 --> 00:12:18,005
Phir usse ek environment variable mein
rakho, jiska naam hai ANTHROPIC API KEY.

194
00:12:18,225 --> 00:12:23,789
SDK isse automatically padh leta hai,
toh key aapke code mein kabhi nahi dikhti.

195
00:12:24,139 --> 00:12:28,789
Key ko kabhi code, chat,
screenshot, ya git commit mein paste mat karo.

196
00:12:29,009 --> 00:12:33,603
Agar key leak ho jaaye, toh turant
Console mein delete karo aur nayi banao.

197
00:12:33,953 --> 00:12:35,456
Abhi key nahi hai?

198
00:12:35,676 --> 00:12:37,039
Koi baat nahi.

199
00:12:37,259 --> 00:12:41,144
Iss module ka sab kuch
offline mode mein bhi chalta hai.

200
00:12:41,364 --> 00:12:43,219
Woh abhi samjhati hoon.

201
00:12:44,519 --> 00:12:47,552
API key ko ATM PIN ki tarah socho.

202
00:12:47,772 --> 00:12:52,247
Jiske paas aapka PIN hai, woh
aapka paisa kharch kar sakta hai.

203
00:12:52,467 --> 00:12:58,159
Jiske paas aapki API key hai, woh
aapka API credit kharch kar sakta hai.

204
00:12:58,379 --> 00:13:01,128
Aap PIN card par likhkar nahi rakhte.

205
00:13:01,348 --> 00:13:03,584
Toh key ko bhi code mein mat likho.

206
00:13:04,884 --> 00:13:09,254
Hamesha ki tarah, ek fresh
virtual environment se shuru karo.

207
00:13:09,604 --> 00:13:12,025
Phir anthropic package install karo.

208
00:13:12,245 --> 00:13:17,479
Mai version two point three point zero
pin kar rahi hoon, jis version par yeh course

209
00:13:17,479 --> 00:13:18,414
record hua hai.

210
00:13:18,634 --> 00:13:25,162
SDK ka matlab hai software development
kit, yaani ready made Python code jo API se

211
00:13:25,162 --> 00:13:27,709
baat karna aasaan bana deta hai.

212
