00:27:15,888 --> 00:27:19,173
Har turn question aur
reply, dono append karo.

424
00:27:19,523 --> 00:27:23,114
Har turn ke saath input
tokens aur cost badhte hain.

425
00:27:23,464 --> 00:27:26,747
Isliye pairs mein trim
karo, ya summarise karo.

426
00:27:27,097 --> 00:27:32,334
Agle lesson mein aap output ko
control karoge: length limits, streaming, aur

427
00:27:32,334 --> 00:27:33,436
structured JSON.

428
00:27:34,759 --> 00:27:36,708
Reply lena aasaan hai.

429
00:27:36,928 --> 00:27:43,328
Lekin aisa reply lena jis par aapka
program bharosa kar sake, uske liye thodi care

430
00:27:43,328 --> 00:27:43,952
chahiye.

431
00:27:44,172 --> 00:27:49,865
Iss lesson mein aap reply ki length
control karoge, reply ko banate banate screen

432
00:27:49,865 --> 00:27:55,769
par dikhaoge, free text ki jagah
structured JSON loge, aur un cases ko handle karoge

433
00:27:55,769 --> 00:27:58,018
jahan model jaldi ruk jaata hai.

434
00:27:59,318 --> 00:28:03,927
Aap max tokens use karoge, aur
har baar stop reason check karoge.

435
00:28:04,277 --> 00:28:08,153
Replies ko stream karoge,
taaki interface fast lage.

436
00:28:08,503 --> 00:28:11,973
Structured outputs se validated JSON loge.

437
00:28:12,323 --> 00:28:15,079
Aur refusals ko safely handle karoge.

438
00:28:16,379 --> 00:28:19,024
Har response batata hai ki woh kyun ruka.

439
00:28:19,244 --> 00:28:21,065
Yeh field hai stop reason.

440
00:28:21,415 --> 00:28:26,078
End turn ka matlab: model ne
apna answer naturally poora kiya.

441
00:28:26,428 --> 00:28:31,969
Max tokens ka matlab: aapki limit aa
gayi aur reply beech mein kat gaya, shayad

442
00:28:31,969 --> 00:28:33,302
aadhe sentence par.

443
00:28:33,652 --> 00:28:38,645
Refusal ka matlab: model ne
safety reasons se request mana kar di.

444
00:28:38,995 --> 00:28:44,011
Stop sequence: model ne aapka diya
hua koi custom stop text likh diya.

445
00:28:44,361 --> 00:28:47,875
Tool use: model aapka
koi tool chalana chahta hai.

446
00:28:48,095 --> 00:28:51,068
Yeh agents ka dil hai, Module 5 mein.

447
00:28:51,418 --> 00:28:57,249
Aur pause turn: ek lamba agentic turn
ruka hai, aur aap usse continue kar sakte ho.

448
00:28:58,549 --> 00:29:04,699
Max tokens ko exam ki word limit ki
tarah socho, ek strict invigilator ke saath.

449
00:29:04,919 --> 00:29:09,488
Time khatam, aur invigilator paper
beech sentence mein hi le leta hai.

450
00:29:09,708 --> 00:29:13,756
Model apna answer limit
ke hisaab se plan nahi karta.

451
00:29:13,976 --> 00:29:16,066
Usse bas rok diya jaata hai.

452
00:29:16,286 --> 00:29:19,523
Aur stop reason batata
hai ki aisa hua ya nahi.

453
00:29:20,823 --> 00:29:23,444
Hum ek hi question do baar puchte hain.

454
00:29:23,664 --> 00:29:28,455
Ek baar badi limit ke saath, ek
baar sirf pandrah tokens ke saath.

455
00:29:28,805 --> 00:29:31,303
Pehli run: hazaar tokens ki limit.

456
00:29:31,523 --> 00:29:35,027
Stop reason end turn,
matlab answer complete hai.

457
00:29:35,377 --> 00:29:37,531
Doosri run: pandrah tokens.

458
00:29:37,751 --> 00:29:42,469
Stop reason max tokens, aur
theek pandrah output tokens use hue.

459
00:29:42,689 --> 00:29:44,620
Answer beech mein kat gaya.

460
00:29:44,970 --> 00:29:47,309
Aur yeh check sabse important hai.

461
00:29:47,529 --> 00:29:51,034
Kata hua reply ek normal
string jaisa hi dikhta hai.

462
00:29:51,254 --> 00:29:57,016
Check nahi kiya, toh aap users ko aadha
answer dikha doge, ya aadhe JSON ko parse

463
00:29:57,016 --> 00:29:58,723
karne ki koshish karoge.

464
00:29:59,073 --> 00:30:02,201
Toh max tokens kaam
ke hisaab se kaafi rakho.

465
00:30:02,421 --> 00:30:08,249
Paise bachane ke liye bahut kam mat
rakho, kyunki kata hua answer usually ek retry

466
00:30:08,249 --> 00:30:09,884
ka kharcha karwata hai.

467
00:30:11,184 --> 00:30:12,283
Ab streaming.

468
00:30:12,503 --> 00:30:14,944
Isse online video ki tarah socho.

469
00:30:15,164 --> 00:30:19,983
Bina streaming ke, aap poori movie
download karte ho, phir play karte ho.

470
00:30:20,203 --> 00:30:25,827
Streaming ke saath, video kuch seconds
mein chal padti hai, aur baaki hissa peeche

471
00:30:25,827 --> 00:30:27,062
se aata rehta hai.

472
00:30:27,282 --> 00:30:31,826
Total data utna hi hai, lekin
intezaar bahut achha lagta hai.

473
00:30:33,126 --> 00:30:36,129
Yaad hai, model ek ek
token karke likhta hai.

474
00:30:36,349 --> 00:30:41,784
Bina streaming ke, aapka program poore
reply ka intezaar karta hai, aur screen

475
00:30:41,784 --> 00:30:42,969
khaali rehti hai.

476
00:30:43,319 --> 00:30:48,969
Streaming mein API pieces bhejti rehti
hai jaise jaise woh bante hain, toh text

477
00:30:48,969 --> 00:30:51,258
lagbhag turant dikhne lagta hai.

478
00:30:51,478 --> 00:30:55,405
Total time same, lekin
experience kaafi fast lagta hai.

479
00:30:55,625 --> 00:31:00,304
Bahut lambe replies par streaming
request timeout se bhi bachata hai.

480
00:31:01,604 --> 00:31:07,499
Messages dot stream bilkul create jaise
hi arguments leta hai, aur with ke saath

481
00:31:07,499 --> 00:31:10,299
context manager ki tarah use hota hai.

482
00:31:10,649 --> 00:31:15,604
Text stream text ke chhote pieces
deta hai, jaise jaise woh aate hain.

483
00:31:15,824 --> 00:31:21,252
Hum har piece turant print karte hain,
flush equals True ke saath, taaki woh buffer

484
00:31:21,252 --> 00:31:22,233
mein ruke nahi.

485
00:31:22,583 --> 00:31:28,424
Aur stream khatam hone par get final
message poora message object deta hai, stop

486
00:31:28,424 --> 00:31:32,074
reason aur usage ke
saath, bilkul create ki tarah.

487
00:31:32,294 --> 00:31:36,475
Video mein pieces turant aa
gaye kyunki fake API local hai.

488
00:31:36,695 --> 00:31:39,622
Lekin code path real
streaming wala hi hai.

489
00:31:40,922 --> 00:31:42,594
Ab structured output.

490
00:31:42,814 --> 00:31:45,969
Ek letter aur ek
government form mein fark socho.

491
00:31:46,189 --> 00:31:50,101
Letter mein kuch bhi, kisi
bhi order mein likha ja sakta hai.

492
00:31:50,321 --> 00:31:53,934
Form mein fixed boxes hote
hain: naam yahan, date wahan.

493
00:31:54,154 --> 00:31:57,204
Form ko program bina
guess kiye padh sakta hai.

494
00:31:57,424 --> 00:32:00,911
Structured outputs model
se ek form bharwaate hain.

495
00:32:02,211 --> 00:32:08,108
Agents ko baar baar machine readable
output chahiye: ek quiz, ek plan, ek tool

496
00:32:08,108 --> 00:32:08,788
decision.

497
00:32:09,008 --> 00:32:11,813
Prompt mein sirf JSON maangna fragile hai.

498
00:32:12,033 --> 00:32:15,978
Extra words, galat keys,
ya toota JSON aa sakta hai.

499
00:32:16,328 --> 00:32:19,094
Structured outputs isse fix karte hain.

500
00:32:19,314 --> 00:32:25,695
Aap ek JSON schema dete ho, aur API
reply ko uss schema ke valid JSON tak hi limit

501
00:32:25,695 --> 00:32:26,474
karti hai.

502
00:32:26,694 --> 00:32:32,786
Pydantic class doge, toh SDK schema bhi
banata hai aur reply ko Python object mein

503
00:32:32,786 --> 00:32:34,272
parse bhi karta hai.

504
00:32:35,572 --> 00:32:38,893
Pehle Pydantic classes
se shape describe karo.

505
00:32:39,113 --> 00:32:44,608
Ek question mein text, chaar options,
sahi answer ka index, aur explanation.

506
00:32:44,828 --> 00:32:47,454
Ek quiz mein topic aur questions ki list.

507
00:32:47,674 --> 00:32:50,934
Pydantic par Module 3
mein poora lesson hai.

508
00:32:51,154 --> 00:32:54,045
Abhi inhe typed
dataclasses ki tarah padho.

509
00:32:54,395 --> 00:33:00,431
Yeh Field constraints kehte hain: exactly
chaar options, aur index zero se teen tak.

510
00:33:00,651 --> 00:33:06,465
API ka schema support limited hai, toh
SDK yeh limits field descriptions mein daal

511
00:33:06,465 --> 00:33:10,010
deta hai, aur reply aane
par khud check karta hai.

512
00:33:10,360 --> 00:33:15,776
Phir create ki jagah messages dot
parse call karo, output format mein class do.

513
00:33:16,126 --> 00:33:19,751
Parsed output ek real,
validated Quiz object hai.

514
00:33:19,971 --> 00:33:24,929
Right side dekho: type hai
Quiz, topic HTTP, aur do questions.

515
00:33:25,149 --> 00:33:29,402
Dictionaries mein khodne ki
jagah aap attributes use karte ho.

516
00:33:29,622 --> 00:33:33,331
Offline fake schema valid
placeholder questions deta hai.

517
00:33:33,551 --> 00:33:39,577
Agar reply schema mein fit na ho, toh
SDK validation error raise karta hai, kharab

518
00:33:39,577 --> 00:33:40,680
data nahi deta.

519
00:33:41,980 --> 00:33:43,953
Aakhri case: refusals.

520
00:33:44,173 --> 00:33:50,020
Agar stop reason refusal hai, toh model
ne safety reasons se mana kiya, aur content

521
00:33:50,020 --> 00:33:51,428
khaali ho sakta hai.

522
00:33:51,648 --> 00:33:55,240
Isliye text padhne se
pehle stop reason check karo.

523
00:33:55,460 --> 00:34:01,731
Current models par API ek declined
request ko automatically doosre model par chala

524
00:34:01,731 --> 00:34:02,495
sakti hai.

525
00:34:02,715 --> 00:34:05,006
Iss feature ko fallbacks kehte hain.

526
00:34:05,226 --> 00:34:09,861
Hamara project isse on karta
hai, lesson six mein code dekhoge.

527
00:34:11,161 --> 00:34:12,620
Interview corner.

528
00:34:12,840 --> 00:34:15,596
LLM response ko stream kyun karte hain?

529
00:34:17,946 --> 00:34:23,904
Answer: generation token by token hoti
hai, toh streaming text ko bante hue dikhati

530
00:34:23,904 --> 00:34:24,191
hai.

531
00:34:24,411 --> 00:34:29,848
User ko turant progress dikhta hai,
total time same rehta hai, aur bahut lambe

532
00:34:29,848 --> 00:34:32,008
replies timeout se bachte hain.

533
00:34:32,228 --> 00:34:36,143
Trap: yeh mat bolna ki
streaming se model fast ho jaata hai.

534
00:34:36,363 --> 00:34:39,755
Woh sirf intezaar ko
chhota mehsoos karwati hai.

535
00:34:40,105 --> 00:34:44,810
Doosra question: ek LLM se
reliable JSON kaise lete ho?

536
00:34:47,160 --> 00:34:49,673
Answer: structured outputs use karo.

537
00:34:49,893 --> 00:34:55,816
JSON schema ya Pydantic model do, taaki
reply usi shape mein aaye, object mein parse

538
00:34:55,816 --> 00:35:00,116
karo, aur phir bhi stop
reason aur business rules check karo.

539
00:35:00,336 --> 00:35:04,148
Trap: prompt mein JSON
maango aur regex se theek karo.

540
00:35:04,368 --> 00:35:07,655
Yeh pehle unusual
reply par toot jaata hai.

541
00:35:08,955 --> 00:35:10,212
Practice time.

542
00:35:10,562 --> 00:35:15,644
Pehla: do sabse common stop reasons
kaun se hain, aur dono ka matlab kya hai?

543
00:35:15,994 --> 00:35:20,412
Doosra: stream dot py mein flush
equals True hata do, toh kya hoga?

544
00:35:20,762 --> 00:35:26,043
Teesra: Quiz schema mein ek
difficulty field add karo, easy, medium, ya hard.

545
00:35:26,393 --> 00:35:31,032
Aur scenario: JSON parsing sirf
lambe replies par fail hoti hai.

546
00:35:31,252 --> 00:35:34,236
Pehle kya check karoge, aur fix kya hoga?

547
00:35:41,536 --> 00:35:42,464
Quick check.

548
00:35:42,684 --> 00:35:48,674
Aapka code reply ko JSON ki tarah parse
karta hai, aur lambe reply par fail ho jaata

549
00:35:48,674 --> 00:35:48,959
hai.

550
00:35:49,179 --> 00:35:51,380
Sabse pehle kya check karoge?

551
00:35:57,080 --> 00:35:59,696
Ki stop reason max tokens hai ya nahi.

552
00:35:59,916 --> 00:36:03,540
Kata hua reply JSON ke
beech mein khatam hota hai.

553
00:36:04,840 --> 00:36:05,680
Recap.

554
00:36:05,900 --> 00:36:09,425
Stop reason batata hai ki
reply complete hai ya nahi.

555
00:36:09,645 --> 00:36:11,281
Hamesha check karo.

556
00:36:11,631 --> 00:36:14,361
Responsive output ke liye stream karo.

557
00:36:14,711 --> 00:36:20,164
Validated JSON ke liye messages
dot parse ke saath structured outputs.

558
00:36:20,514 --> 00:36:24,205
Aur content padhne se
pehle refusal handle karo.

559
00:36:24,555 --> 00:36:26,840
Agla lesson: production basics.

560
00:36:27,060 --> 00:36:31,199
Errors, rate limits, retries,
aur yeh sab kitne ka padta hai.

561
00:36:32,530 --> 00:36:35,685
Ek demo jo ek baar
chal jaaye, woh aasaan hai.

562
00:36:35,905 --> 00:36:41,801
Lekin ek program jo network girne par,
rate limit aane par, ya cost badhne par bhi

563
00:36:41,801 --> 00:36:46,188
chalta rahe, uske liye soch
samajhkar design karna padta hai.

564
00:36:46,408 --> 00:36:51,991
Yeh lesson woh production basics
sikhata hai jo har AI application ko chahiye.

565
00:36:53,291 --> 00:36:58,309
Aap API ke error types
pehchanoge, aur har ek ke liye kya karna hai.

566
00:36:58,659 --> 00:37:01,392
Errors ko sahi order mein catch karoge.

567
00:37:01,742 --> 00:37:04,889
Rate limits aur
automatic retries samjhoge.

568
00:37:05,239 --> 00:37:08,796
Aur har call ki cost
calculate aur control karoge.

569
00:37:10,096 --> 00:37:12,789
Pehle what: kaun kaun se errors aate hain.

570
00:37:13,009 --> 00:37:17,035
HTTP status code batata
hai ki problem kis taraf hai.

571
00:37:17,385 --> 00:37:21,073
Four hundred ya four oh
four: aapki request galat hai.

572
00:37:21,293 --> 00:37:25,868
Koi galat parameter, ya model
ka naam jo exist hi nahi karta.

573
00:37:26,088 --> 00:37:29,400
Retry se kuch nahi
hoga, request theek karo.

574
00:37:29,750 --> 00:37:32,804
Four oh one aur four
oh three: key ki problem.

575
00:37:33,024 --> 00:37:35,922
Key missing hai, galat
hai, ya permission nahi hai.

576
00:37:36,142 --> 00:37:38,445
Retry mat karo, key theek karo.

577
00:37:38,795 --> 00:37:42,140
Four twenty nine: aapne
rate limit cross kar di.

578
00:37:42,360 --> 00:37:45,504
Yahan rukna aur retry
karna bilkul sahi hai.

579
00:37:45,854 --> 00:37:51,705
Five hundred wale errors, five twenty
nine overloaded bhi, server side problems

580
00:37:51,705 --> 00:37:53,334
hain, aksar temporary.

581
00:37:53,554 --> 00:37:55,645
Thoda rukkar retry karo.

582
00:37:55,995 --> 00:38:00,418
Aur network errors ya timeouts:
koi proper response aaya hi nahi.

583
00:38:00,638 --> 00:38:02,872
Yeh bhi retry karne layak hain.

584
00:38:04,172 --> 00:38:05,068
Ab how.

585
00:38:05,288 --> 00:38:11,017
Sirf iss demo ke liye hum automatic
retries band karte hain, taaki har error hamare

586
00:38:11,017 --> 00:38:12,259
code tak pahunche.

587
00:38:12,609 --> 00:38:14,639
Call ek try block ke andar hai.

588
00:38:14,989 --> 00:38:20,116
Phir hum specific exception classes
catch karte hain, sabse specific pehle.

589
00:38:20,336 --> 00:38:23,812
Pehle authentication
error, phir rate limit error.

590
00:38:24,162 --> 00:38:30,331
API status error har HTTP error ki
parent class hai, toh jo bacha hai woh yeh pakad

591
00:38:30,331 --> 00:38:32,636
leti hai, status code ke saath.

592
00:38:32,856 --> 00:38:37,795
Connection errors HTTP errors hain
hi nahi, isliye unki alag class hai.

593
00:38:38,015 --> 00:38:43,481
Agar parent class pehle catch karoge,
toh specific handlers kabhi chalenge hi nahi.

594
00:38:43,831 --> 00:38:48,092
Bina kisi failure ke, ek
normal placeholder reply aata hai.

595
00:38:48,312 --> 00:38:49,985
Right side par wahi hai.

596
00:38:51,285 --> 00:38:57,343
Bina kuch tode errors dikhane ke liye,
fake API ek environment variable padhti hai,

597
00:38:57,343 --> 00:39:00,117
jo batata hai ki kaise fail karna hai.

598
00:39:00,467 --> 00:39:04,278
Four oh one ka message
banta hai: check your API key.

599
00:39:04,628 --> 00:39:07,134
Four twenty nine ka: rate limited.

600
00:39:07,484 --> 00:39:13,224
Aur five twenty nine, overloaded server,
general status handler tak pahunchta hai.

601
00:39:14,524 --> 00:39:19,786
Rate limit ka matlab: har account ke
liye ek limit hai ki ek minute mein kitni

602
00:39:19,786 --> 00:39:22,485
requests aur kitne tokens bhej sakte ho.

603
00:39:22,705 --> 00:39:25,827
Limit cross hui, toh
four twenty nine aata hai.

604
00:39:26,047 --> 00:39:29,968
Iska solution samjho ek
busy dost ko call karne se.

605
00:39:30,188 --> 00:39:31,550
Line busy hai.

606
00:39:31,770 --> 00:39:34,395
Aap har second redial nahi karte.

607
00:39:34,615 --> 00:39:38,075
Thoda rukte ho, aur har
baar thoda zyada rukte ho.

608
00:39:38,295 --> 00:39:43,831
Aur agar hazaar log yahi kar rahe hain,
toh thodi randomness unhe ek hi second par

609
00:39:43,831 --> 00:39:45,856
wapas call karne se rokti hai.

610
00:39:47,156 --> 00:39:48,605
Dry run dekho.

611
00:39:48,825 --> 00:39:50,751
Try one: four twenty nine.

612
00:39:50,971 --> 00:39:54,995
Lagbhag aadha second
ruko, thodi randomness ke saath.

613
00:39:55,345 --> 00:39:57,824
Try two: five hundred, server error.

614
00:39:58,044 --> 00:40:00,237
Ab lagbhag ek second ruko.

615
00:40:00,457 --> 00:40:02,122
Wait dugna ho gaya.

616
00:40:02,472 --> 00:40:03,966
Try three: success.

617
00:40:04,186 --> 00:40:05,730
Reply use karo.

618
00:40:07,030 --> 00:40:11,642
Achhi khabar yeh hai ki
Anthropic SDK yeh sab already karta hai.

619
00:40:11,862 --> 00:40:15,035
Max retries se aap isse control karte ho.

620
00:40:15,255 --> 00:40:18,222
Default do hai, aur zero se band hota hai.

621
00:40:18,572 --> 00:40:21,177
Normal case mein call succeed hoti hai.

622
00:40:21,397 --> 00:40:24,749
Ab dekhte hain jab
fake API pehle fail kare.

623
00:40:26,049 --> 00:40:30,951
Yahan fake API pehle four twenty
nine deti hai, phir five hundred.

624
00:40:31,171 --> 00:40:36,802
ANTHROPIC LOG ko info karne se dikhta
hai SDK kya kar raha hai: thoda rukta hai,

625
00:40:36,802 --> 00:40:41,659
retry karta hai, phir thoda zyada
rukta hai, phir retry, aur success.

626
00:40:41,879 --> 00:40:45,036
Hamare code mein ek
bhi extra line nahi lagi.

627
00:40:46,336 --> 00:40:48,390
Production ke kuch aur rules.

628
00:40:48,610 --> 00:40:51,472
Ek timeout set karo
jo aapke liye theek ho.

629
00:40:51,692 --> 00:40:54,174
SDK ka default das minute hai.

630
00:40:54,394 --> 00:40:56,792
Lambe replies ke liye stream karo.

631
00:40:57,142 --> 00:41:00,017
Kuch fail ho, toh request ID log karo.

632
00:41:00,237 --> 00:41:04,264
Isse pata chalta hai
exactly kaunsi request fail hui.

633
00:41:04,614 --> 00:41:10,155
Har app aur environment ki alag key
